.TH OSDOCTOR 1 "2026-05-30" "osdoctor 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
osdoctor \- Linux desktop health checks for Arch/Hyprland systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B osdoctor
.RI < COMMAND >
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B osdoctor
runs a set of read-only health checks against the host system, the
package manager, the systemd service state, and the desktop session, then
prints a grouped report. It is aimed at Arch Linux systems running Hyprland
and Omarchy-style configurations, but the system, service, and package checks
are useful on any systemd-based Arch install.
.PP
All checks are read-only: osdoctor never changes system state, and normal
scans do not require root.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Run every check group (System, Services, Packages, Desktop).
.TP
.B system
Run only the system checks (kernel, root disk space, /tmp, memory).
.TP
.B services
Run only the service checks (failed system and user units).
.TP
.B packages
Run only the package checks (pacman lock, log, orphans).
.TP
.B desktop
Run only the desktop checks (Wayland session, Hyprland socket, Hyprland bind
commands, Waybar scripts).
.TP
.B version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit results as a JSON document instead of the human-readable report.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Treat warnings as failures for the purpose of the exit code. The displayed
status labels are unchanged.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read configuration from
.I PATH
instead of the default file. A missing or invalid file is an error. Use
.B \-\-config /dev/null
to force the defaults. May be given once.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
osdoctor reads an optional TOML file,
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/osdoctor/config.toml
(default
.IR ~/.config/osdoctor/config.toml ),
or the file given with
.BR \-\-config .
Every key is optional, and a missing default file means defaults. Example:
.PP
.nf
.RS
# ~/.config/osdoctor/config.toml - every key is optional.

[thresholds]
disk_warn_gb = 10          # WARN when / has less free space than this
disk_fail_gb = 2           # FAIL when / has less free space than this
memory_warn_percent = 10   # WARN when less than this % of memory is available

[checks]
# <check-id> = "off" | "warn" | "fail"
#   off   the check does not run and is not reported
#   warn  a WARN or FAIL result from this check is reported as WARN
#   fail  a WARN or FAIL result from this check is reported as FAIL
waybar-scripts = "warn"
# pacman-log = "off"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Each key in
.B [checks]
is a check ID and takes one of three modes:
.B off
(the check does not run and is not reported),
.B warn
(a WARN or FAIL result is reported as WARN), or
.B fail
(a WARN or FAIL result is reported as FAIL). OK and SKIP results are never
changed. The
.B \-\-strict
flag is applied after the modes.
.PP
The
.B [thresholds]
keys and their defaults are:
.B disk_warn_gb
(10),
.B disk_fail_gb
(2), and
.B memory_warn_percent
(10).
.PP
Invalid configuration (a missing
.B \-\-config
file, a syntax error, an unknown key or check ID, or a bad value) is reported
as
.RI \(lq "osdoctor: message" \(rq
on standard error and exits with status 3. The
.B help
and
.B version
commands never read the configuration.
.SH "CHECK STATUS LEVELS"
Each check reports one of:
.B OK
(healthy),
.B WARN
(worth attention),
.B FAIL
(a definite problem), or
.B SKIP
(not applicable in this environment).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
All checks passed (no warnings, no failures).
.TP
.B 1
One or more warnings, but no failures.
.TP
.B 2
One or more failures (or, under \fB\-\-strict\fR, one or more warnings).
.TP
.B 3
Invalid usage or an internal/tooling error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_TYPE
Inspected by the Wayland session check.
.TP
.B HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE ", " XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Used to locate the Hyprland IPC socket.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Directory holding the Hyprland and Waybar configuration files when set to an
absolute path; otherwise
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B HOME
Expands
.B ~
in configuration paths and commands; relative Hyprland exec commands resolve
against it, as Hyprland runs them from the home directory.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, disables colorized output. Color is also disabled automatically when
standard output is not a terminal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/osdoctor/config.toml
Optional configuration file (see CONFIGURATION).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hypr/hyprland.conf
Parsed for \fBexec\fR bind commands, including any files pulled in with
\fBsource =\fR (resolved recursively, relative to the including file).
Hyprland \fB$variables\fR and environment variables are expanded, and the
program each command runs (as \fBsh \-c\fR would, after any
\fINAME\fR=\fIvalue\fR prefixes) must resolve to an executable. Commands that
start with a shell builtin or operator are not checked.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/waybar/config.jsonc ", " $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/waybar/config
The programs of command fields (\fBexec\fR, \fBexec\-*\fR, \fBon\-*\fR) that
point at local scripts must exist. JSONC comments are ignored.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pacman/db.lck
Presence indicates a locked pacman database.
.TP
.I /var/log/pacman.log
Checked for existence and readability.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run all checks:
.B osdoctor scan
.TP
Machine-readable output:
.B osdoctor scan \-\-json
.TP
Only the desktop checks, failing on warnings:
.B osdoctor desktop \-\-strict
